NAME
    gcloud alpha kms retired-resources - manage retired resources

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha kms retired-resources COMMAND [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) A retired resource represents a deleted key version.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     describe
        (ALPHA) Get metadata for a given retired resource.

     list
        (ALPHA) List the retired resources within a location.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist. These variants are also available:

        $ gcloud kms retired-resources

        $ gcloud beta kms retired-resources

